# Supabase Configuration
# Get these from your Supabase project dashboard: https://app.supabase.com
# Project Settings → API

# Your Supabase project URL (e.g., https://xxxxx.supabase.co)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Your Supabase anon/public key (this is the "anon public" key, safe for client-side use)
VITE_SUPABASE_KEY=your_publishable_key_here

# Dev mode - bypasses settings lock (set to true during development)
VITE_DEV_MODE=false

# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to .env:  cp .env.example .env
# 2. Create a Supabase account at https://supabase.com (free tier works)
# 3. Create a new project
# 4. Go to Project Settings → API
# 5. Copy your "Project URL" and paste it as VITE_SUPABASE_URL above
# 6. Copy your "anon public" key and paste it as VITE_SUPABASE_KEY above
# 7. Save the .env file (it's in .gitignore and will never be committed)
# 8. Run npm install && npm run build
#
# Single-User Deployment Notes:
# This extension is designed for ONE user (you). After Supabase setup:
# 1. Create ONE user account via Supabase Dashboard (Authentication → Users → Add user)
# 2. Store credentials securely in password manager
# 3. Session persists across restarts via chrome.storage.local
# 4. SDK auto-refreshes tokens - no re-login needed
#
# To set up session on new device, run this in browser console (F12) once:
#
# const email = 'your@email.com';
# const password = 'your_password';
# const supabaseUrl = 'YOUR_URL';  // Same as VITE_SUPABASE_URL
# const supabaseKey = 'YOUR_KEY';  // Same as VITE_SUPABASE_KEY
#
# fetch(`${supabaseUrl}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password`, {
#   method: 'POST',
#   headers: { 'apikey': supabaseKey, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
#   body: JSON.stringify({ email, password })
# })
